WEBVTT

1
00:00:51.120 --> 00:00:56.360
Hello everyone. I'm going to speak today on behalf of my manager

2
00:00:56.360 --> 00:00:59.560
because he's not really strong in English.

3
00:00:59.560 --> 00:01:04.400
So I'll try to keep his ideas and present everything to you.

4
00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:08.150
I hope you don't mind.

5
00:01:10.120 --> 00:01:13.350
So, imagine the situation.

6
00:01:13.880 --> 00:01:18.160
You have developed a product you are happy

7
00:01:18.160 --> 00:01:21.680
with its properties, you have set up production and you launch

8
00:01:21.680 --> 00:01:26.920
it onto the market. And then after some time, the packaging starts to

9
00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:33.160
swell. You check the formula, change the proportions and conduct all

10
00:01:33.160 --> 00:01:36.030
the tests, but it still doesn't work.

11
00:01:36.960 --> 00:01:40.790
And then you decide to turn to artificial intelligence.

12
00:01:41.760 --> 00:01:45.470
AI gives you a good explanation and specific recommendations.

13
00:01:46.400 --> 00:01:49.550
And that raises an important question:

14
00:01:50.440 --> 00:01:55.520
How quickly can we really apply the recommendations that AI has

15
00:01:55.520 --> 00:02:02.212
given us? For our company, this question

16
00:02:02.212 --> 00:02:06.042
came up while we were working on air-dry modeling clay.

17
00:02:07.812 --> 00:02:14.452
This was the search for a

18
00:02:14.452 --> 00:02:16.482
solution that lasted 18 months.

19
00:02:17.052 --> 00:02:21.572
For 12 months, we were testing suggestions from ChatGPT and Gemini

20
00:02:21.572 --> 00:02:23.402
that they had given us.

21
00:02:23.892 --> 00:02:29.172
And only after 12 months of work did we bring in a chemist to

22
00:02:29.172 --> 00:02:31.602
start real work and testing.

23
00:02:33.292 --> 00:02:36.122
Today we want to talk not about the clay itself,

24
00:02:36.692 --> 00:02:41.162
but about the experience it brought to our business.

25
00:02:43.732 --> 00:02:48.602
Our company focuses on creative kits,

26
00:02:49.212 --> 00:02:51.722
board games and educational games.

27
00:02:52.132 --> 00:02:58.532
And we provide the whole line, from the beginning of formulation

28
00:02:58.532 --> 00:03:02.842
to production and quality control of the product.

29
00:03:11.412 --> 00:03:14.482
So, the main problem.

30
00:03:16.252 --> 00:03:18.082
At first, everything was fine.

31
00:03:18.852 --> 00:03:23.092
The clay had the right consistency, it retained its color,

32
00:03:23.092 --> 00:03:25.492
it was easy to shape.

33
00:03:25.492 --> 00:03:30.692
But during storage, we noticed a problem: the volume

34
00:03:30.692 --> 00:03:32.682
of the packaging gradually increased.

35
00:03:33.892 --> 00:03:38.122
It happened without any external inflation.

36
00:03:38.892 --> 00:03:43.572
For us, it was a serious issue because the customer sees only

37
00:03:43.572 --> 00:03:48.652
the packaging. And if the packaging is damaged or doesn't look

38
00:03:48.652 --> 00:03:54.692
good, it's natural for a person to question the quality

39
00:03:54.692 --> 00:03:58.372
of a product. So, we started looking for the cause.

40
00:03:58.372 --> 00:04:01.442
We changed the proportions, we tested new formulations,

41
00:04:01.934 --> 00:04:05.004
we decided to change components,

42
00:04:06.254 --> 00:04:09.844
and changed different technological processes,

43
00:04:10.454 --> 00:04:12.964
but the swelling kept happening.

44
00:04:18.014 --> 00:04:21.764
That's when we decided to use AI in our research.

45
00:04:22.574 --> 00:04:27.934
So, we presented the problem to AI and started exploring different

46
00:04:27.934 --> 00:04:33.214
possibilities. AI suggested various additives and they were quite

47
00:04:33.214 --> 00:04:34.164
convincing,

48
00:04:35.294 --> 00:04:39.524
and its recommendations for changes were

49
00:04:41.974 --> 00:04:44.004
something that you would believe in.

50
00:04:44.574 --> 00:04:50.724
And that's where we learned our main lesson

51
00:04:51.694 --> 00:04:53.484
in all this, that

52
00:05:01.214 --> 00:05:04.734
AI can give you the answer in a few seconds,

53
00:05:04.734 --> 00:05:10.534
but to test it, you need to create a sample and that requires a long

54
00:05:10.534 --> 00:05:15.254
line of production. So, it requires new raw materials,

55
00:05:15.254 --> 00:05:21.774
it requires new decisions and even time for the team

56
00:05:21.774 --> 00:05:28.454
to work. So, we had to run all these experiments and

57
00:05:28.454 --> 00:05:31.644
review them to get the evidence that it's really working.

58
00:05:40.774 --> 00:05:46.254
So, we tested starch, talc, microcalcite and other substances and

59
00:05:46.254 --> 00:05:52.454
how the clay behaved under different temperature conditions, and we

60
00:05:52.454 --> 00:05:58.534
used an incubator to control every condition and

61
00:05:58.534 --> 00:06:01.524
understand exactly when the problem happened.

62
00:06:02.454 --> 00:06:08.765
So, we gradually eliminated hypotheses

63
00:06:09.695 --> 00:06:16.055
and when we had a convincing explanation for that,

64
00:06:16.055 --> 00:06:20.495
we understood that it's not the same as proof, because artificial

65
00:06:20.495 --> 00:06:24.095
intelligence can provide us a very logical answer,

66
00:06:24.095 --> 00:06:28.455
but only in real-world production can you see if it's working or

67
00:06:28.455 --> 00:06:29.355
not.

68
00:06:38.695 --> 00:06:43.525
So, the main idea is that the decision always remains with people

69
00:06:44.175 --> 00:06:49.975
and we can accept or reject the result, prepare reports,

70
00:06:49.975 --> 00:06:54.415
and then only the management team decides which directions are worth

71
00:06:54.415 --> 00:06:55.315
testing.

72
00:07:05.295 --> 00:07:08.935
It's really easy to talk about artificial intelligence and it's

73
00:07:08.935 --> 00:07:12.495
much harder to talk about the people who spent one and a half years

74
00:07:12.495 --> 00:07:17.045
opening the same sample and seeing it's not working.

75
00:07:17.495 --> 00:07:22.855
After 10 unsuccessful attempts, it was easy to lose

76
00:07:22.855 --> 00:07:28.125
motivation, and only the work of our employees

77
00:07:28.975 --> 00:07:33.285
helped us: they were testing, analyzing,

78
00:07:33.695 --> 00:07:38.575
and it was systematic work that gradually brought us to a promising

79
00:07:38.575 --> 00:07:43.175
hypothesis. We assumed that the formulation was missing a component

80
00:07:43.175 --> 00:07:46.975
necessary to maintain the product's

81
00:07:46.975 --> 00:07:48.765
stability after packaging.

82
00:07:49.575 --> 00:07:53.615
So, this changed the direction of our research and at this point,

83
00:07:53.615 --> 00:07:56.165
specifically, we brought in a chemist.

84
00:08:06.615 --> 00:08:10.777
So, we kept the original formulation as a basis and added the necessary

85
00:08:10.777 --> 00:08:14.337
component and adjusted the preparation process.

86
00:08:14.337 --> 00:08:19.017
In particular, we reviewed the

87
00:08:19.017 --> 00:08:23.817
preparation of borax. Using glycerin alone did not help and didn't

88
00:08:23.817 --> 00:08:25.287
provide sufficient dissolution.

89
00:08:25.977 --> 00:08:30.767
And so, we added another chemical compound to adjust the formula.

90
00:08:39.497 --> 00:08:41.447
So, as a result, we had

91
00:08:42.417 --> 00:08:45.847
stable packaging and the clay kept its original properties.

92
00:08:46.457 --> 00:08:52.257
And we learned how AI actually works in a real business

93
00:08:52.257 --> 00:08:53.157
situation.

94
00:08:59.617 --> 00:09:04.497
We understood that in our business, AI is certainly not

95
00:09:04.497 --> 00:09:06.937
the one who is in charge of making decisions.

96
00:09:06.937 --> 00:09:13.807
It's the one who gives us hypotheses to explore,

97
00:09:14.937 --> 00:09:19.217
and then we can see more possibilities and ask better questions to

98
00:09:19.217 --> 00:09:22.207
reach a new, promising

99
00:09:23.577 --> 00:09:30.137
hypothesis. So, AI can provide us the answer within seconds,

100
00:09:30.137 --> 00:09:34.297
but it's only people who are in charge of making decisions and only

101
00:09:34.297 --> 00:09:40.417
their experience and their ideas and decisions can verify the

102
00:09:40.417 --> 00:09:42.127
information. Thank you.
